  "result": "Done! Added complete payment recording functionality:\n\n**New module - src/payments.js:**\n\n1. **recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date})**\n   - Records a payment against an invoice\n   - Creates `invoice.payments` array on first payment\n   - Automatically transitions invoice status:\n     - 'issued' \u2192 'partially_paid' after first payment\n     - 'partially_paid' \u2192 'paid' when fully paid\n   - Validates: amount must be positive integer\n   - Prevents overpayment\n   - Returns immutable new invoice\n\n2. **balanceDue(invoice)**\n   - Calculates amount still owed\n   - Formula: invoice.total - sum of payments\n   - Clamped at 0 (never negative)\n\n**Validation & Errors:**\n- **NOT_ISSUED**: Can only record payments on 'issued' or 'partially_paid' invoices\n- **AMOUNT_INVALID**: Amount must be positive integer (in cents)\n- **OVERPAYMENT**: Payment cannot exceed remaining balance\n\n**Example:**\n```javascript\n// Create and issue invoice\nconst invoice = issueInvoice(draft, []).value;\n// Total due: \u20ac102.85\n\n// Record partial payment\nconst r1 = recordPayment(invoice, { amount: 50000, date: '2025-10-20' });\n// Status: 'partially_paid', Balance due: \u20ac52.85\n\n// Record remaining payment\nconst r2 = recordPayment(r1.value, { amount: 5285, date: '2025-10-25' });\n// Status: 'paid', Balance due: \u20ac0\n```\n\n**Tests added:** 14 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Balance calculations with/without payments\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Multiple payments on same invoice\n- Validation (zero, negative, fractional amounts)\n- Overpayment prevention\n- Payment on different invoice statuses\n- Immutability guarantee\n\n**Test results:** \u2705 All 142 tests pass (128 existing + 14 new)",
